From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juan Pablo Lassala <jpablolassala@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 09:37:53 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] typing-break: Do not start under Camino

The plugin starts mate-typing-monitor, which watches the keyboard through
X11. Under Camino, the Wayland compositor for MATE, it sees only the keys
typed into XWayland applications, so its breaks come at the wrong times.

When MATE_WM_NAME is Camino, do not start the manager. Without that
variable, nothing changes.
---
 plugins/typing-break/msd-typing-break-plugin.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/plugins/typing-break/msd-typing-break-plugin.c b/plugins/typing-break/msd-typing-break-plugin.c
index 5b9233c..3e3194a 100644
--- a/plugins/typing-break/msd-typing-break-plugin.c
+++ b/plugins/typing-break/msd-typing-break-plugin.c
@@ -71,6 +71,14 @@ impl_activate (MateSettingsPlugin *plugin)
         gboolean res;
         GError  *error;
 
+        /* mate-typing-monitor watches the keyboard through X11, and under
+         * Camino, the Wayland compositor for MATE, it would see the keys of
+         * XWayland applications only and count a break that is not one. */
+        if (g_strcmp0 (g_getenv ("MATE_WM_NAME"), "Camino") == 0) {
+                g_debug ("Not activating typing_break plugin under Camino");
+                return;
+        }
+
         g_debug ("Activating typing_break plugin");
 
         error = NULL;
